To the Office of FOIA Services,

U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission



I am submitting this Freedom of Information Act request on behalf of WhyDRS=
, a nonprofit public-interest association.=20



I respectfully request all records related to the Chicago Mercantile Exchan=
ge (CME Group) trading outage that began on the night of Thursday, November=
 27, 2025 and continued into the morning of Friday, November 28, 2025.=20



We would appreciate all SEC internal and external records concerning the ou=
tage, in any form or medium.





Specifically, please search for and provide all responsive records (includi=
ng but not limited to):

Internal email correspondence and other electronic communications (includin=
g attachments) among SEC employees or officials discussing the outage.

Meeting agendas, minutes, notes, or transcripts from any SEC meetings or ca=
lls where the outage was addressed.

Internal memoranda, situation reports, incident reports, analysis documents=
, presentations, or other staff reports prepared by SEC personnel concernin=
g the outage.

Records of communications (emails, letters, call logs, messages, etc.) betw=
een SEC staff or officials and external parties =E2=80=93 including CME Gro=
up representatives, other regulators (e.g. the CFTC), self-regulatory organ=
izations, trading firms, clearinghouses, or other market participants =E2=
=80=93 that pertain to the outage.

Logs or transcripts of phone calls, text messages, instant messages, or oth=
er communications involving SEC personnel regarding the outage.

Any other documents or records (electronic or paper) related to the CME out=
age.




I authorize fees up to $250 to avoid delays.



I respectfully request a fee waiver. WhyDRS is a nonprofit entity focused o=
n public education about market structure, investor protection, and systemi=
c risk. The materials requested concern:

A major operational event affecting a federally regulated financial market =
operator.

Federal oversight of CME Group, clearing operations, and related systemic-r=
isk management.

Matters the public has a strong and documented interest in understanding.


The requested records concern direct and identifiable operations or activit=
ies of the Federal Government, including regulatory response, monitoring, a=
nd risk-assessment pertaining to a significant market-infrastructure failur=
e. Disclosure will contribute substantially to public understanding, as I w=
ill publish all non-exempt materials and analysis openly for investors, jou=
rnalists, researchers, and the general public.



This request is not being made for commercial purposes. WhyDRS does not sel=
l data or research and receives no economic benefit from publication.





=E2=B8=BB



Contact Information



Name: John Wooten

Organization: WhyDRS

Telephone: 341-465-6469

Email: mailto:john@whydrs.org=20



=E2=B8=BB



Please confirm receipt of this request. If you need clarification or wish t=
o discuss narrowing or prioritizing search scopes, I am available at any ti=
me.



Thank you for your assistance and for your service to the public.


In good faith,
John Wooten

WhyDRS
